; --sort-xacts with an empty argument is an error, as --sort with one is.
; Before the period-sorting flag moved out of --sort-xacts, an empty value
; was how normalize_period marked a period report, so a user's empty
; --sort-xacts was silently taken for that marker: alone it did nothing,
; and beside -S it dropped the report-wide sort.

2024/01/05 Payee A
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/20 Payee B
    Expenses:Rent    $5.00
    Expenses:Food    $1.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg --sort-xacts '' -> 1
__ERROR__
Error: No argument provided for --sort-xacts
end test

test reg -S amount --sort-xacts '' -> 1
__ERROR__
Error: No argument provided for --sort-xacts
end test
